      "claim": "N-(N-benzylpiperidin-4-yl)-2-[18F]fluorobenzamide showed good brain uptake in mice, supporting the benzylpiperidine CNS-penetration motif.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "[11C]MC80 showed high initial brain uptake in wild-type mice, providing additional in vivo evidence for CNS access in a related dimethoxyaryl scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is donepezil, an established CNS-penetrant drug, and all provided experimental records from close analogs, metabolites, and related benzylpiperidine/dimethoxyaryl compounds show positive BBB penetration with no contradictory evidence.",
